{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, a clear ~4.2% gain over rna-only config_001 (0.485/0.464), confirming that adding the image modality is beneficial. However, we have zero evidence on whether multiprofile (multiple profiles per cell) provides additional signal beyond singleprofile. Question: config_018 extends the best-performing config_016 by switching to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation, holding all other settings constant (pca_n2000, resnet50, concat). This isolates the effect of the profile setting in the multimodal context. Why this is the best next experiment: the profile axis is a fundamental design decision that gates an entire half of the search space (configs 018-051 vs 016-017, 022-023, etc.). Testing it early in the multimodal setting—where we already have a positive signal—maximizes information value: if multiprofile helps, we validate a large region of configurations; if it does not, we can concentrate remaining budget on singleprofile variants and encoder/fusion choices. This is the most informative single experiment under the limited budget."
}

